{"name":"Canary Wharf","hex":"#91a1b5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Canary Wharf","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A business district on the Isle of Dogs, borough of Tower Hamlets, Greater London, England ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Canary_Wharf"}],"entries":[{"title":"Canary Wharf","blocks":[{"text":"Canary Wharf is a privately owned central business district in London, England, located in the Isle of Dogs, Tower Hamlets. With the City of London and the West End, it constitutes one of the main financial centres in the United Kingdom and the world, and it is home to many of the world’s major financial corporations, including the headquarters of more than 150 major businesses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Canary_Wharf_from_entrance_to_Limehouse_Basin_-_2022-04-03.jpg/330px-Canary_Wharf_from_entrance_to_Limehouse_Basin_-_2022-04-03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canary_Wharf"},{"title":"Canary Wharf (ward)","blocks":[{"text":"Canary Wharf is an electoral ward in the London Borough of Tower Hamlets. The ward was first used in the 2014 elections. It returns councillors to Tower Hamlets London Borough Council. It covers a wider area of Tower Hamlets beyond the privately owned Canary Wharf."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canary_Wharf_(ward)"},{"title":"Wharf","blocks":[{"text":"A wharf, quay, staith, or staithe is a structure on the shore of a harbor or on the bank of a river or canal where ships may dock to load and unload cargo or passengers. Such a structure includes one or more berths, and may also include piers, warehouses, or other facilities necessary for handling the ships. Wharves are often considered to be a series of docks at which boats are stationed. A marginal wharf is connected to the shore along its full length."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Houston_Ship_Channel_Barbours_Cut.jpg/330px-Houston_Ship_Channel_Barbours_Cut.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wharf"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Canary_Wharf_Wide_View_2%2C_London_-_July_2009.jpg/500px-Canary_Wharf_Wide_View_2%2C_London_-_July_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Canary_Wharf_Wide_View_2%2C_London_-_July_2009.jpg/1280px-Canary_Wharf_Wide_View_2%2C_London_-_July_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Canary_Wharf_Wide_View_2%2C_London_-_July_2009.jpg/500px-Canary_Wharf_Wide_View_2%2C_London_-_July_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACanary_Wharf_Wide_View_2%2C_London_-_July_2009.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Greenwich_and_Canary_Wharf_%283%29_-_2022-04-24.jpg/500px-Greenwich_and_Canary_Wharf_%283%29_-_2022-04-24.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Greenwich_and_Canary_Wharf_%283%29_-_2022-04-24.jpg/1280px-Greenwich_and_Canary_Wharf_%283%29_-_2022-04-24.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Greenwich_and_Canary_Wharf_%283%29_-_2022-04-24.jpg/500px-Greenwich_and_Canary_Wharf_%283%29_-_2022-04-24.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreenwich_and_Canary_Wharf_(3)_-_2022-04-24.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Cabot_Square%2C_Can